#
# Instance example: site 'archive' (s2): git's GLOBAL configuration inside its agent
# TURN unit. The turn HOME is root's, so a turn cannot write this file (or any other at HOME
# level) and plant a setting every later turn of the site would read. It repeats the system
# file's directives.
# The agent CLI runs git itself in the workspace, whose .git the unit masks; git's discovery
